   "text": "Checking for a known issue behind this NumPy probe failure \u2014 searching library docs and reports.\nI found several reports with the same import error \u2014 now opening them to verify the match.\nOne source already matches exactly \u2014 checking one more to confirm before I answer.\nKnown issue: pyarrow 26 requires NumPy 2 but its wheel declares no NumPy dependency, so resolvers keep NumPy 1.26.4 and import fails with `ImportError: pyarrow requires NumPy 2.0 or newer, found 1.26.4`. The `datasets` dependency permits pip to install PyArrow 26 while retaining NumPy 1.26.4, causing failure during import.\n\n{\"status\": \"found\", \"sources\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Automodel/pull/4244\", \"title\": \"fix(ci): keep pyarrow compatible with CUDA build numpy by akoumpa \u00b7 Pull Request #4244 \u00b7 NVIDIA-NeMo/Automodel\", \"why\": \"Reports the identical ImportError for pyarrow requiring NumPy 2.0 or newer, found 1.26.4 with PyArrow 26 and NumPy 1.26.4.\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5372\", \"title\": \"[CI] Preserve NumPy 1.x support by constraining PyArrow by sanketpurandare \u00b7 Pull Request #5372 \u00b7 pytorch/torchtitan\", \"why\": \"Documents that datasets permits PyArrow 26 with NumPy 1.26.4 retained, causing import failure because PyArrow 26 requires NumPy 2.\"}]}"
